{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-72733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x=y+1 \\\\ x-y=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-72733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=1 \\\\ x-y=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-72733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "accd8fff95b0dbeadacb9cd38ae26fe1ab7cf46fa5191fd1db1f96a6a46c559f"} {"question" "q-72733" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-72733" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-72733" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-102808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3=y \\\\ 3y=4x+2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-102808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=3 \\\\ -4x+3y=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-102808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "accd8fff95b0dbeadacb9cd38ae26fe1ab7cf46fa5191fd1db1f96a6a46c559f"} {"question" "q-102808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_s