per/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "accd8fff95b0dbeadacb9cd38ae26fe1ab7cf46fa5191fd1db1f96a6a46c559f"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{14}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320806" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 4x=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $6$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 4x+y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-320847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "accd8fff95b0dbeadacb9cd38ae26fe1ab7cf46fa5191fd1db1f96a6a46c559f"} {"question" "q-320847" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/