sented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-6$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $4$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-6$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-321441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5a219fd4624b0e8ec5b280b41273d7f7f929ca7c15d6ea288b8e085cfe2daf2"} {"question" "q-321441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041555/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "accd8fff95b0dbeadacb9cd38ae26fe1ab7cf46fa5191fd1db1f96a6a46c559f"} {"question